---
import Layout from '@boring-sites/design/Layout.astro';
const siteName = 'Word Unscrambler';
---
<Layout
  title="About"
  description="About the Word Unscrambler — a fast, no-signup anagram solver."
  siteName={siteName}
  logoVariant="word-unscrambler"
>
  <article class="container-prose py-12">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">About</h1>
    <div class="prose mt-8 dark:prose-invert">
      <p>
        <strong>Word Unscrambler</strong> is a fast, no-signup anagram solver. It's part of the <a href="https://github.com/ksjpswaroop/boring-sites">boring-sites</a> portfolio — small, fast utility sites built with the same design system.
      </p>
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>
        The tool runs entirely in your browser. The word list is bundled at build time (no API calls, no server roundtrip). When you type letters, the engine:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>Normalizes the input (uppercase, A–Z only, max 15 chars)</li>
        <li>Looks up every word whose sorted-letters signature is a subset of your input</li>
        <li>Returns results sorted by Scrabble score (or length, or alpha)</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        <strong>Real-time.</strong> No click-to-submit. The list updates as you type.
      </p>
      <h2>What we don't do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No login, no account, no saved history</li>
        <li>No server-side processing</li>
        <li>No tracking beyond cookieless analytics (Plausible)</li>
        <li>No ads between results</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Open source</h2>
      <p>The full source is on <a href="https://github.com/ksjpswaroop/boring-sites">GitHub</a>. Audit it, fork it, run it locally.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
